No slash'em knowledge here, but in vanilla:

If you just keep gathering them, as in the huge
surplus in the Gnomish Mines, eventually the
most-created ones should prevail, the +0 ones, by
quite a margin.

Alternatively you can stack them, remove any
individual names some might have, zap them with a
wand of cancellation, making them _all_ +0 uncursed,
and they will stack (by type) when you pick them up.

Otherwise, daggers just plain won't stack, and
there's no cure for it, if they differ in:

* individual name, or lack thereof

* B/U/C status

* Enchantment level

* type of dagger (orcish, runed, "plain", silver, ...)

